micro-ecc, a small ECDH and ECDSA implementation by Kenneth MacKay.

Source:   https://github.com/kmackay/micro-ecc
Version:  v1.2 (commit 541b3a78026420a3e369c4c9281c396b5e531113, 2024-11-13)
Licence:  BSD 2-clause, see LICENSE.txt

Only the C sources are kept (uECC.c, uECC.h, uECC_vli.h, types.h,
curve-specific.inc, platform-specific.inc), unmodified. The assembly files are
for 32-bit ARM and AVR, which Haiku does not build this for.

Used by the Bluetooth kit for LE Secure Connections pairing (P-256 ECDH):
src/kits/bluetooth/LEP256.c includes uECC.c with only secp256r1 enabled and
its symbols hidden, and sets getentropy() as the random number source. The
results are checked against the Bluetooth Core specification's sample data by
src/tests/kits/bluetooth/le_sc_crypto_test.
